 /* ---- 0122: read-only GMU inventory ----
- * GMU registers are GMU_WORD(n)=4*n from the GMU base; the live DT node
- * qcom,gmu has reg 0x3d68000 size0x34000 (its unit address differs). The
- * inventory observes what the boot loader left: CM3 reset/boot state,
- * firmware init result, the always-on counter (19.2MHz crystal), the
- * power/clock status, RPMh power state and the HFI/AO handshake. It runs
- * inside the 0121 clock stage while the GMU tree is up and CX is live,
- * before the branches are restored, so the AHB access is clocked. Read
- * only: no GMU write, no firmware load, no GPU core or SMMU access.
+ * GMU register addresses come from the pinned a6xx_gmu.xml dword offsets,
+ * which are relative to the GPU base, not to the GMU node: physical =
+ * 0x3d00000 + (dword << 2), so the GMU-relative offset for peridot is
+ * (dword << 2) - (0x3d68000 - 0x3d00000) = (dword << 2) - 0x68000. The live
+ * DT node qcom,gen7-gmu has reg 0x3d68000 size0x37000 (its unit address
+ * differs). 0122 used the redwood-relative offsets (0x14000 class) and the
+ * first read hit the hole at 0x3d7c000: external abort, diagnostic reset
+ * recovered. The inventory observes what the boot loader left: CM3
+ * reset/boot state, firmware init result, the always-on counter (19.2MHz
+ * crystal), the power/clock status, RPMh power state and the HFI/AO
+ * handshake. It runs inside the 0121 clock stage while the GMU tree is up
+ * and CX is live, before the branches are restored, so the AHB access is
+ * clocked. Read only: no GMU write, no firmware load, no GPU core or SMMU
+ * access.
  */
-#define PGPU_GMU_CM3_SYSRESET 0x14000u
-#define PGPU_GMU_CM3_BOOT_CONFIG 0x14004u
-#define PGPU_GMU_CM3_FW_INIT_RESULT 0x14070u
